' 4. One program connection
' The reference for this protocol. The pseudo code in 4-program-connection.md
' details each numbered step.

@startuml program-connection

skinparam style strictuml
!pragma teoz true

box "Sandbox" #LightBlue
participant "program" as Program
end box

box "Tally proxy" #LightBlue
participant "proxy" as Proxy
participant "writer" as Writer
database "log" as Log
end box

box "Upstream" #LightBlue
participant "server" as Server
end box

note over Proxy
given the settings and the secrets, loaded at startup (see 1):
<latex>H</latex> the listed hosts, <latex>K</latex> the keys,
each key <latex>k</latex> with <latex>k.\mathtt{placeholder}</latex>, <latex>k.\mathtt{host}</latex>, <latex>k.\mathtt{header}</latex>;
<latex>r</latex> the request being handled
end note

note over Proxy, Log
if a line can't be written:
reply 503, and the proxy stops (see 2)
end note

Program o-> Proxy : opens a connection

group while the connection is open

  Program -> Proxy : request

  rnote over Proxy #d1d5ef
    1. read the head and check it
    follows the strict HTTP rules
  end rnote

  rnote over Proxy #d1d5ef
    2. call 3. decide request: the first case that applies
  end rnote

  rnote over Proxy #ffffff
    // <latex>\scriptstyle h_r</latex> host in the URL, <latex>\scriptstyle r.\mathtt{Host}</latex> the list of Host header values, both normalized (lowercase, :80 if no port),
    // <latex>\scriptstyle r[h]</latex> the values of the header lines named <latex>\scriptstyle h</latex> in <latex>\scriptstyle r</latex>, <latex>\scriptstyle \#_r(h)</latex> their number,
    // <latex>\scriptstyle K_r = \{k \in K \mid k.\mathtt{placeholder} \text{ occurs in } r[k.\mathtt{header}]\}</latex> the keys found, <latex>\scriptstyle \rho</latex> the reason of a refusal
    <latex>\scriptstyle d = \begin{cases} \mathtt{refuse}(\mathtt{host\_mismatch}) & \quad\text{if } r.\mathtt{Host} \neq [h_r] \cr \mathtt{refuse}(\mathtt{malformed\_request}) & \quad\text{if } \exists k \in K_r,\ \#_r(k.\mathtt{header}) > 1 \cr \mathtt{refuse}(\mathtt{host\_not\_allowed}) & \quad\text{if } \exists k \in K_r,\ k.\mathtt{host} \neq h_r \cr \mathtt{refuse}(\mathtt{host\_not\_allowed}) & \quad\text{if } K_r = \emptyset \wedge h_r \notin H \cr \mathtt{pass} & \quad\text{if } K_r = \emptyset \cr \mathtt{release}(K_r) & \quad\text{otherwise} \end{cases}</latex>
  end rnote

  alt if <latex>d = \mathtt{refuse}(\rho)</latex>

    rnote over Proxy #d1d5ef
      3. refuse
    end rnote

    ref over Proxy, Writer, Log : call 2. log the refuse line, wait until on disk
    Proxy --> Program : refusal: status + reason

    rnote over Proxy #d1d5ef
      close the connection
    end rnote

  else <latex>d = \mathtt{release}(K_r)</latex> or <latex>d = \mathtt{pass}</latex>

    rnote over Proxy #d1d5ef
      4. read the rest of the body,
      then log the decision
    end rnote

    break if the body doesn't arrive in full
      rnote over Proxy #d1d5ef
        refuse as in 3, with <latex>\rho = \mathtt{incomplete\_request}</latex>
      end rnote
    end

    ref over Proxy, Writer, Log : call 2. log the release or pass line, wait until on disk

    note right of Writer
      nothing is sent to the
      server before this answer
    end note

    rnote over Proxy #d1d5ef
      5. rewrite the request and swap
      each placeholder for its real key
    end rnote

    Proxy -> Server : request, with the real keys

    alt if the server can't be reached, or the shutdown time limit cuts in

      ref over Proxy, Writer, Log : call 2. log the upstream_error line, wait until on disk
      Proxy --> Program : 502 or 504 (none when cut off)

    else

      rnote over Proxy #d1d5ef
        6. relay the response
      end rnote

      ref over Program, Proxy, Server : call 5. relay response

    end

    rnote over Proxy #d1d5ef
      7. keep the connection for the next request
    end rnote

    rnote over Proxy #ffffff
      <latex>\scriptstyle \mathtt{keep} \iff \text{the last reply to } r \text{ is complete} \ \wedge\ \text{it doesn't say } \mathtt{Connection:\ close}</latex>
    end rnote

  end

end

@enduml
